<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gwanggaeto the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">374–413</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Gwanggaeto of Goguryeo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gwanggaeto the Great was the nineteenth king of Goguryeo, reigning from 391 to 413. He conquered wide lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> from the Later Yan and the Khitan, defeated Baekje, and sent an army to help Silla against Wa (Japanese) and Gaya forces in 400. His deeds are recorded on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwanggaeto-stele">Gwanggaeto Stele</a>, erected by his son Jangsu in 414 near the old capital in modern Ji'an, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gwanggaeto-the-great.jpg" alt="Gwanggaeto the Great" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EditQ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwanggaeto_Stele_5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
